{composer: Peters }


https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kfrJvZamYns  (Capo 1) (MC2/3)

There’s also a version in (G).  You'll have to play it capo'd at the 6th fret but it's much easier to play, and I think prettier, too.

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (FaddG).

TIP:  The (G) (D7sus4) - (G) is a little awkward but in this case is really an augmentation of the (G).  Just keep the bottom finger planted on the 1st string and bring your index and ring fingers down to the 2nd string/1st fret and 3rd string/2nd fret respectively.  Move the index finger sort of like you're setting up for a (C) and the middle finger will naturally follow. Then return to the (G) like a pivot. 

TIP:  The (FaddG) will follow an (F) so just keep form and add your pinky to the bottom string/3rd fret.  
   
  
